<title>UK: CRICKET-FOURTH ASHES TEST STARTS AFTER RAIN DELAY.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-FOURTH ASHES TEST STARTS AFTER RAIN DELAY.</headline>
<dateline>LEEDS, England 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain which had already held up the toss subsequently delayed the start of play by 70 minutes in the fourth Ashes test on Thursday.</p>
<p>Australia won the toss and put England in to bat at Headingley but light rain fell just as the match was about to start 50 minutes late.</p>
<p>Play finally got under way following a further 20 minutes delay.</p>
</text>
